        "title": "Propagating the 0.0.4 release identifier",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "setup.py executes version.py into a dictionary and passes __version__ to setup(version=...). The changed string therefore supplies 0.0.4 as the package base version.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_1fa789ef968b46ff9294e867bc24279a",
              "call_f57197456dac44ce83c7c023ef040e1e"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "compile_model imports __version__ and writes it as quantization_config.version in the output config.json. Conversions reaching that write record 0.0.4; this edit does not rewrite existing artifacts.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_d9ab5ca0901841858e6c21c9f9a694af",
              "call_f57197456dac44ce83c7c023ef040e1e"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The manually dispatched build workflow parses version.py for release naming, yielding tag v0.0.4 and release name 0.0.4. Upload remains conditional on parsing not returning None and the release input being '1'; the input defaults to '0', so the bump itself does not initiate publication.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_e5a44ec7de054f6a9f6a40f65c2ba643",
              "call_f57197456dac44ce83c7c023ef040e1e"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
